726 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (When you look at a bank account, you see a balance. The bank keeps an internal ledger and simply increases or decreases a number whenever you make a transaction. Bitcoin works differently. The network does not store balances. Instead, it stores pieces of bitcoin called UTXOs \(Unspent Transaction Outputs\), which are transaction outputs that have not yet been spent.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [496 0 R]
>>
endobj
